r the finite monotone operator family. The critic at most raises an abstract worry that hardness could be displaced rather than removed, but displacement would require showing that the selector or the operator-lattice pass hides an equivalent NP-hard subproblem; the critic provides no such reduction. Nothing in the target's specification entails that the operator-lattice pass or the finite selection is worst-case non-polynomial, and the critic has not established otherwise. The polynomial cost guarantee is therefore not shown to be violated.

